{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JMQaR5TfWwzNeXLyQ2e2SN","type":"tool_result","content":"\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n\n\\subsection{Full per-family results}\n\\label{sec:si_family}\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Per-family held-out results. Errors are mean absolute log errors. The best-bound error is derived as our predictor's error minus the paired difference $\\Delta$. CIs are 95\\% two-level bootstrap intervals for the paired difference; the evaluator reports no intervals for the per-family errors themselves.}\n\\label{tab:family}\n\\small\n\\begin{tabular}{lrrrrc}\n\\toprule\nFamily & Held-out & Our error & Best bound (derived) & Paired $\\Delta$ & 95\\% CI of $\\Delta$ \\\\\n\\midrule\nLollipop & 18 & 0.164 & 0.275 & $-0.111$ & $[-0.225,\\ 0.013]$ \\\\\nPath & 9 & 0.092 & 0.476 & $-0.384$ & $[-0.502,\\ -0.238]$ \\\\\nBinary tree & 9 & 0.163 & 0.806 & $-0.643$ & $[-0.833,\\ -0.414]$ \\\\\nRandom tree & 16 & 0.062 & 0.855 & $-0.793$ & $[-0.865,\\ -0.703]$ \\\\\nCycle & 9 & 0.129 & 1.255 & $-1.126$ & $[-1.258,\\ -0.963]$ \\\\\nStar & 9 & 0.056 & 1.404 & $-1.347$ & $[-1.678,\\ -0.952]$ \\\\\n2D grid & 5 & 0.364 & 1.871 & $-1.507$ & $[-1.743,\\ -1.210]$ \\\\\nRandom 3-regular & 16 & 0.059 & 2.146 & $-2.088$ & $[-2.303,\\ -1.859]$ \\\\\nComplete & 9 & 0.357 & 2.433 & $-2.076$ & $[-2.520,\\ -1.608]$ \\\\\nErd\\H{o}s--R\\'enyi & 16 & 0.381 & 2.453 & $-2.072$ & $[-2.494,\\ -1.626]$ \\\\\n\\midrule\nFamily-weighted mean & 116 & 0.183 & 1.397 & $-1.214$ & $[-1.303,\\ -1.130]$ \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n% @evidence[[analysis/derived_metrics.json#per_family]] @evidence[[analysis/roster.json#final_eval]]\n\\end{table}\n86:\\label{fig:overview}\n198:\\label{fig:plane}\n227:\\label{fig:family}\n230:Figure~\\ref{fig:family} and Table~\\ref{tab:family} in the Supplementary Information address the second research question. The predictor's own error varies by a factor of almost seven across families. % @evidence[[analysis/derived_metrics.json#per_family_error_spread_ratio]]\n237:The paired gain over the best bound (Figure~\\ref{fig:family}b) has a 95\\% interval excluding zero in 9 of 10 families. % @evidence[[analysis/derived_metrics.json#n_families_ci_excludes_zero]]\n251:Sorting families by the best bound's error (Figure~\\ref{fig:family}a) gives an almost monotone pattern in the gains. The derived best-bound error is smallest on lollipops (0.275) and paths (0.476), the two families whose shapes are closest to the extremal constructions for the cubic and spanning-tree bounds. It is largest on complete (2.433) and Erd\\H{o}s--R\\'enyi graphs (2.453). % @evidence[[analysis/derived_metrics.json#per_family]]\n262:For a practitioner with a small graph from one of the evaluated families, the six-statistic predictor gives a point estimate typically within about 20\\% of the expected cover time. It is more reliable on tree-like, regular and star-like graphs than on dense, random or grid graphs. When a guaranteed budget is required, the generic bounds remain the right tool, and their slack can be read off Figure~\\ref{fig:family}a: for lollipop-like graphs the cheaper of the two bounds is already accurate to within a typical factor of about 1.3.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b15765f-ba82-4d49-aaa3-a4d557e16332","uuid":"5fcf4d25-58b7-44c1-9dbc-049687811af9","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:45:50.612Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n\n\\subsection{Full per-family results}\n\\label{sec:si_family}\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Per-family held-out results. Errors are mean absolute log errors. The best-bound error is derived as our predictor's error minus the paired difference $\\Delta$. CIs are 95\\% two-level bootstrap intervals for the paired difference; the evaluator reports no intervals for the per-family errors themselves.}\n\\label{tab:family}\n\\small\n\\begin{tabular}{lrr